<title>CHILE: Chile government bans British beef imports.</title>
<headline>Chile government bans British beef imports.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile said on Wednesday it has banned the import of British beef and beef sub-products as the result of &quot;mad cow&quot; disease which has affected British cattle herds.</p>
<p>The prohibition, published in the government gazette Diario Oficial, extends to other products including &quot;prime materials and medicines which are...made with prime materials coming from cattle originating in the United Kingdom.&quot;</p>
<p>The ban is largely symbolic as Chile imports little beef from Britain. Most of its meat imports are from Argentina and Uruguay.</p>
</text>
